    uint32_t     ttl;

    IgnoreError(otDnsAddressResponseGetHostName(aResponse, hostName, sizeof(hostName)));

    OutputFormat("DNS response for %s - ", hostName);
    ...
}
```

`IgnoreError` ignores the failure, and `hostName` is passed to `OutputFormat` as a `%s` string. Since `hostName` is not NUL-terminated (the name filled the entire buffer), this is a stack buffer over-read.

